Review written to `docs/reviews/defaults-data/defdata-07-zip-load-parameters.md`.

**Summary of findings**:

- **2 High**: (1) Scheduled load reactive power formula uses `pf` as raw scalar instead of `tan(acos(pf))` — causes e.g. resistive loads to report Q=P instead of Q=0. (2) HARES coefficient assignment (real→real, reactive→reactive) diverges from OCHRE (which swaps them), causing 15–24% power differences at non-nominal voltages — undocumented.

- **2 Medium**: Compressor pf values (0.96–0.97) are at the top of the range for modern equipment but may not represent older stock. No frequency sensitivity parameters.

- **3 Low**: All Z+I+P sums verified at exactly 1.0 (no violations). Dishwasher has asymmetric real (constant-impedance) vs reactive (constant-power) ZIP parameters. No load-time validation in the deserialization struct.
